Add `-vsemantic=<filename>` to trace function body analysis requests

The `-vsemantic` switch records which expressions and scheduling operations
request function body analysis, together with starts, finishes, skips and
deferrals. It helps investigate attribute inference and forward references.

---
dmd -vsemantic=analysis.trace -c example.d
---

Tracing is disabled by default and writes to a separate file. The output is a
debugging aid; its format may change. It does not change inference or scheduling.
